# Milestone: M3
# Covers: two Realms have isolated bindings; var defined in one realm is not
#         visible in another.
#
# Driven by the chk-host-driver (## host: directives): the single-pass urbi -i
# REPL path manages one realm internally and cannot demonstrate cross-realm
# isolation.  The driver creates two named realms, binds x in each, and reads
# x back from each to show the bindings do not leak.
#
# r1: bind x = 1 ; r2: bind x = 2 ; then read x under each realm.
## host: realm r1
## host: run var x = 1
## host: realm r2
## host: run var x = 2
[00000001] 1
[00000002] 2
## host: realm r1
## host: run x
## host: realm r2
## host: run x
[00000003] 1
[00000004] 2
